A||N||8||red88formula||New owner, high idle||||1||
Z||000000||red88formula||05-29-2001||03:17 PM||||I am new to the message board and am now a new owner of an 88 Formula with only 33k original miles.  The first thing I get to address is the car's high idling problem.  I was getting code 35 for IAC valve...now that I replaced that, it still idles high (usually 1500-2k RPM) and now sets code 24 for speed sensor (which doesn't make sense w/car sitting still).  The cat converter has also been removed...I don't know if this would contribute to a high idle.  When you press on the EGR, it hardly has any effect on the car...so maybe vaccuum leak?  Let me know what you guys think...<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero Formula, Bright Red, 5spd, 33k miles, Kenwood KDC-MP8017<p>[This message has been edited by red88formula (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||05-29-2001||03:30 PM||||Welcome to the forum!  There is lots 'o info here with problems/solutions from A - Z.  I think your problem is most likely a vacuum leak (usually caused by a cracked EGR tube but not always).  Use the search function and look for 'high idle' in the technical postings and you should get back an hour or more of reading on that single topic.<BR>GL & keep us posted||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-29-2001||03:33 PM||||vacuum leak is the most common cause of a high idle. follow the egr tube up to the plenium and look at it carefully - use a mirror and flashlight if you have to.<P>  If you cant see any crack look for black areas in one of the rippled bands - black indicates an exhaust leak when the erg is open = vacuum leak the rest of the time.<P>  Another way is to spray wd40 where you think there might be a vacuum leak with the engine running - if you spray a leak it will alter the idle - slows it down I think. <P>use a dental mirror and flashlite and follow each vacuum line across the engine end to end and make sure they are all attached - do the wd40 thing as much as you can.<P>  it should idle at 900rpm in neutral and about 800 in drive with an auto tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-29-2001||03:35 PM||||dont forget the vacuum lines that run along the trunk side of the engine compartment, and the ones up onthe firewall too. there are metal ones in both places that tend to corrode.||||reg||1
Z||000004||85Josh||05-29-2001||03:35 PM||||Welcome aboard! The 24 code just means that the engine is running, and the car isn't moving, Some ECM's do this, and some don't. The high idle is most likely vaccum leaks, check the ogre's cave (link at top and bottom of page) under engine-vaccum leaks. That page helped me find some pretty obscure problems in my 85 four cyl. Good luck, and by the way, the advice to use the search function is both excellent advice, and something you will hear a lot.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||05-29-2001||04:00 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!! There are a lot of Fiero owners on here who live around you (Chadman, 87ECO5, Boilermaker, Fiero56, WilliamThornIII, etc........I'm sure they would be glad to help you out in person if you need it.........post a message for 87ECO5 and see what happens..........(by the way, I used to live in Cincinnati - still get there from time to time and I have a Med. Red Met. '87GT back there.....)<P>Terry<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                 </A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||red88formula||05-29-2001||05:54 PM||||Cool, thanks for all the suggestions.  Glad to hear there are some local owners on here.  I know a few others in the area outside of the board who are in clubs.<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero Formula, Bright Red, 5spd, 33k miles, Kenwood KDC-MP8017||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||07-12-2001||03:16 PM||||<B>red88formula</B> - did you ever solve your problem?||||reg||5
Z||000008||red88formula||07-12-2001||03:22 PM||||Sorry I didn't post an update...<P>Yeah, the problem is fixed.  There was a crack in the EGR tube.  New tube and replaced the EGR while I was at it and it's running fine.<P>Thanks for the help!||||reg||1
